# The annotations of Trush block 0's contents ($7F58-$9AFF): the loading screen and the code that fades it in. The
# single source of src/disk/screen/*.asm (kit/mkgame.py --image). Boot's Start runs block 0 at $7E2C (it unpacks
# these bytes and returns), copies the screen to bank 7 and calls ShowLoadingScreen.

@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the screen's bitmap
@equ $5800 Attrs 768 ; the attribute file
@equ $B000 FadeEnd ; one past the last darkened attribute copy (seven 768-byte copies from $9B00)

@module screen ; the loading screen and its fade-in
@about The screen at $8000 is the loading picture (src/res/screen/loading.scr, 6912 bytes as a .scr). ShowLoadingScreen shows the bitmap under black attributes, makes seven copies of the attributes from dark to full and shows them in that order, 6 frames apart.
$7F58 c ShowLoadingScreen ; attributes black, the bitmap shown, then the attribute copies from dark to full every 6 frames
> MakeFades writes the seven copies to $9B00, $9E00 ... $AE00, the darkest first and the last one equal to the picture's own attributes. The loop copies 768 bytes a step from $9B00 on and stops when HL reaches FadeEnd.
$7F62 ; 6 frames between the steps
$7F68 ; one attribute copy to the screen
$7F76 c MakeFades ; attributes black, the bitmap to the screen, the darker attribute copies built at $9B00
> Each copy takes B from the ink and C from the paper of every cell (not below 0) and keeps BRIGHT and FLASH: B runs 6 down to 0 and C 48 down to 0 in steps of 8, so the first copy is the darkest and the seventh takes nothing. The two OR $00 instructions get the new ink and paper written into their operands.
$7F94 ; one copy of the 768 attributes at $9800
$7FB0 SetInk ; the cell's BRIGHT and FLASH with the darkened ink (the operand written above) ...
$7FB2 SetPaper ; ... and paper
@isub $7F9F LD (SetInk+1),A
@isub $7FAA LD (SetPaper+1),A
$7FC4 c ClampInk ; A = B (the ink not taken below 0)
$7FC6 c ClampPaper ; A = C
$7FC8 t Credit ; " PROGRAM BY MIKE BLUM ": never printed
$7FDE s Spare ; zeros to the screen
$8000 b LoadingScreen ; the loading screen: bitmap and attributes
@res screen/loading.scr
